# Ticketing System (TKT-001)

**Phase:** 0.5 — Final design (documentation only; no implementation in this phase).

**Purpose:** Define the canonical contract for multi-tenant member support ticketing across Tour Ops clubs — domain model, lifecycle, authorization, API, UX, testing, and rollout — before contract or schema implementation.

**Principle:** Ticketing is a **platform capability** with **workspace-configurable** categories and enablement. Every read and write is **tenant-bound**, **backend-enforced**, and **fail-closed**. PostgreSQL + RLS is the only persistence path; memory storage is forbidden for ticketing data.

---

## 1. Purpose

**DECISION:** Clubs need a first-party support channel for members to ask questions, report registration/payment/profile issues, and track operator responses — without email, WhatsApp, or external helpdesk tools in MVP.

**FACT:** The platform already provides:

- Multi-tenant identity (`User`, `UserTenant`) — `apps/api/prisma/schema.prisma:537-564`
- JWT member sessions on Portal (PCMS-001) — `docs/standards/member-session-portal-authority.mdoc`
- Operator sessions on Web (`atour_op_session`) — same standard §1
- RLS via `withTenantRls` — `apps/api/src/db/with-tenant-rls.ts:16-39`
- CASL operator surfaces — `packages/workspace-sdk/src/auth/operator-surface.ts:6-17`
- Booking command-center inbox UX — `apps/web/src/features/bookings/bookings-command-center-shell.tsx`
- Portal `/me/*` BFF pattern — `apps/portal/app/api/me/wallet/route.ts:29-53`

**INFERENCE:** Ticketing reuses these primitives; it does not introduce a parallel auth or storage model.

---

## 2. Scope

### In scope (MVP)

| Area | Detail |
| ---- | ------ |
| Surfaces | Member Portal (`apps/portal`), Operator Web (`apps/web`) |
| Actors | `member`, `viewer` (read-only), `admin`, `owner` |
| Core flows | Create ticket, list, read, public reply, internal note, assign, status/priority change, reopen |
| Persistence | PostgreSQL tables + RLS (`app.current_tenant_id`) |
| Categories | Stable `categoryCode` + manifest labels |
| Priority | `low`, `normal`, `high`, `urgent` |
| Audit | `TicketEvent` (product timeline) + `AuditEvent` (compliance) |

### Workspace coverage

**DECISION:** Ticketing is **not Denali-specific**. Any workspace plugin may opt in via manifest `workspaceTicketing.supported: true` (manifest field to be added in Phase 1 — design only here).

**INFERENCE:** Default for new workspaces: `supported: false` until explicitly enabled (fail-closed), matching wallet `defaultModuleEnabledWhenUnset: false` pattern in `packages/workspaces/denali/workspace.manifest.json:224-227`.

---

## 3. Non-goals

**OUT OF SCOPE (MVP):**

| Item | Rationale |
| ---- | --------- |
| Marketing surface | Anonymous users — PCMS-001; no member session |
| Platform admin cross-tenant inbox | No product evidence; tenant isolation risk |
| Memory / in-memory ticketing store | **DECISION:** forbidden — wallet already rejects memory (`apps/api/src/workspace-wallet/wallet-repository.factory.ts:14-16`) |
| Notifications (in-app, email, SMS, WhatsApp) | Phase 7; member inbox currently in-memory (`apps/api/src/notifications/member-notification-inbox.repository.ts:19`) |
| Attachments (binary upload) | Phase 7; future contract documented §7.4 |
| SLA timers and escalations | Phase 7; JSM SLA is separate from queues (Atlassian community — not used as architecture SoT) |
| AI auto-reply, automation engine | OUT OF SCOPE |
| Live chat, omnichannel inbox | OUT OF SCOPE |
| Knowledge base, public forum | OUT OF SCOPE |
| Bulk actions on operator inbox | Phase 6+ enhancement |
| Category builder UI | MVP uses manifest-defined codes only |
| Tags | Phase 7+ |
| `new`, `on_hold`, `awaiting_operator` statuses | Simplified lifecycle §8 |

---

## 4. Personas

| Persona | Role | App | MVP capabilities |
| ------- | ---- | --- | ---------------- |
| Club member | `member` | Portal | Create, list own, read own, public reply, reopen `resolved` |
| Club viewer | `viewer` | Portal | List/read own tickets only; no create/reply |
| Club operator | `admin` | Web | Full tenant inbox; reply, internal note, assign, status, priority |
| Workspace owner | `owner` | Web | Same as admin + archive/delete (if enabled) |
| Platform admin | — | — | **OUT OF SCOPE** MVP |

**UNKNOWN:** Whether `viewer` should see tickets for tours they are registered on but did not create — MVP limits to **own tickets only** (`requesterUserId`).

---

## 5. Architecture placement

```text
┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│ apps/portal                          apps/web                            │
│  /me/tickets/*                       /tickets/*                          │
│  BFF /api/me/tickets/*  ──────────►  operatorApiFetch → API              │
└──────────────────────────────┬──────────────────────────────────────────┘
                               │
                               ▼
┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│ apps/api                                                                 │
│  resolveTenantContextFromRequest (tenant-kernel.ts:35-84)               │
│  requireOperatorSession (operator routes)                                │
│  runWithHttpRequestContext (bind-request-context.ts:39-88)               │
│  ticketing.service → withTenantRls (with-tenant-rls.ts:16-39)            │
└──────────────────────────────┬──────────────────────────────────────────┘
                               │
         ┌─────────────────────┼─────────────────────┐
         ▼                     ▼                     ▼
packages/ticketing-    packages/ticketing-    packages/ticketing-
http-contracts          core                    http
(Zod DTOs)              (lifecycle, authz)      (route handlers)
         │                     │                     │
         └─────────────────────┴─────────────────────┘
                               │
                               ▼
              workspace.manifest.json → workspaceTicketing { supported, categories }
```

**DECISION:** Package layout mirrors Wallet/Booking:

| Package | Responsibility |
| ------- | -------------- |
| `@app-tour/ticketing-http-contracts` | Zod schemas, wire types, error codes |
| `@app-tour/ticketing-core` | Pure domain: transitions, permission checks, validation |
| `@app-tour/ticketing-http` | HTTP handlers; host ports pattern (`wallet-http`) |
| `apps/api/src/workspace-ticketing/` | Prisma repositories, service wiring, route registration |

**DECISION:** Add operator surfaces to `OperatorSurface` in Phase 1:

```text
operator.tickets.read
operator.tickets.mutate
operator.tickets.assign
```

**FACT:** Existing surfaces — `packages/workspace-sdk/src/auth/operator-surface.ts:6-17`. Viewer uses member JWT on Portal with `role: viewer` — `packages/workspace-sdk/src/auth/auth-context.ts:2`.

---

## 6. Tenant isolation

### Rules (MUST)

1. **Every** ticketing query includes `tenantId` from authenticated context — never from unvalidated body/query alone.
2. **Every** persistence call uses `withTenantRls(tenantId, …)` — `apps/api/src/db/with-tenant-rls.ts:16-39`.
3. **Never** fetch by `ticketId` alone; always `WHERE tenant_id = $auth.tenantId AND id = $ticketId`.
4. Member routes filter `requesterUserId = auth.userId` unless operator role.
5. `assigneeUserId` must reference a `UserTenant` row with `tenantId = auth.tenantId` and `status = ACTIVE`.
6. `relatedTourId` / `relatedRegistrationId` must be validated to belong to the same `tenantId` before persist.
7. **DECISION:** Memory driver MUST NOT implement ticketing repositories. API boot MUST reject ticketing routes when `resolveStorageDriver() === "memory"` (same posture as wallet).

### RLS

**DECISION:** New tables `tickets`, `ticket_messages`, `ticket_events` get:

- `ENABLE ROW LEVEL SECURITY` + `FORCE ROW LEVEL SECURITY`
- Policy: `tenant_id = current_setting('app.current_tenant_id', true)::uuid`

**FACT:** Session variable — `packages/tenant-kernel/src/rls/session.ts:5-7`.

### IDOR mitigations

| Risk | Mitigation | Severity |
| ---- | ---------- | -------- |
| Cross-tenant ticket read | RLS + auth.tenantId | P0 |
| Member reads another member's ticket | `requesterUserId` filter | P0 |
| Internal note leaked to member API | `visibility = public` filter on member routes | P0 |
| Assignee from another tenant | `UserTenant` membership check | P1 |
| Related tour from another tenant | FK validation query under RLS | P1 |

---

## 7. Domain model

### 7.1 Ticket

**DECISION:** No `description` column on `Ticket`. Initial message is the first `TicketMessage` with `visibility: public`.

**DECISION:** No `workspaceType` column on `Ticket`. Resolve from tenant registry at read time (`resolveWorkspaceTypeForTenant`) — `apps/api/src/http/bind-request-context.ts:55-57`.

| Field | Type | Required | Notes |
| ----- | ---- | -------- | ----- |
| `id` | UUID | yes | PK; global UUID acceptable — isolation via tenantId + RLS |
| `tenantId` | UUID | yes | FK → `tenants.id`; RLS key |
| `requesterUserId` | UUID | yes | FK → `users.id`; member who opened ticket |
| `assigneeUserId` | UUID | null | FK → `users.id`; validated via `UserTenant` |
| `categoryCode` | string(64) | yes | Stable code; label from manifest |
| `priority` | enum | yes | `low` \| `normal` \| `high` \| `urgent`; default `normal` |
| `status` | enum | yes | §8 |
| `subject` | string(200) | yes | |
| `relatedTourId` | UUID | null | Same-tenant tour FK |
| `relatedRegistrationId` | UUID | null | Same-tenant registration FK |
| `lastActivityAt` | timestamptz | yes | Updated on message/status change |
| `resolvedAt` | timestamptz | null | Set when → `resolved` |
| `closedAt` | timestamptz | null | Set when → `closed` |
| `rowVersion` | int | yes | Optimistic concurrency; default 1 |
| `createdAt` | timestamptz | yes | |
| `updatedAt` | timestamptz | yes | |

**Indexes:**

```text
@@index([tenantId, status, lastActivityAt(sort: Desc)])
@@index([tenantId, requesterUserId, createdAt(sort: Desc)])
@@index([tenantId, assigneeUserId, status])
@@unique([tenantId, id])
```

**Soft delete:** **OUT OF SCOPE** MVP. Use `closed` terminal state. `archive` = operator sets `closed` (no separate flag in MVP).

### 7.2 TicketMessage

| Field | Type | Required | Notes |
| ----- | ---- | -------- | ----- |
| `id` | UUID | yes | PK |
| `tenantId` | UUID | yes | RLS |
| `ticketId` | UUID | yes | FK composite `(tenantId, ticketId)` |
| `authorUserId` | UUID | yes | From JWT — never from client body |
| `visibility` | enum | yes | `public` \| `internal` |
| `body` | text | yes | Max 10_000 chars MVP |
| `idempotencyKey` | string(128) | null | Per-message dedup |
| `createdAt` | timestamptz | yes | Monotonic ordering |

**DECISION:** `authorRole` is **not stored**. Derived at read time from `UserTenant.role` for `authorUserId` or from auth context at write time for authorization only.

**Indexes:**

```text
@@index([tenantId, ticketId, createdAt(sort: Asc)])
@@unique([tenantId, ticketId, idempotencyKey])  -- where idempotencyKey IS NOT NULL
```

**Rules:**

- Member API returns only `visibility = public`.
- Operator API returns all messages.
- POST message on `status = closed` → **409** `TICKET_CLOSED`.
- POST message on `status = resolved` by member → allowed (becomes reopen flow §8) OR auto-transition to `open` — **DECISION:** member reply on `resolved` auto-transitions to `open` and appends message (Zendesk solved-reopen pattern).

### 7.3 TicketEvent vs AuditEvent

**DECISION:** Use **both**:

| Store | Purpose | Consumer |
| ----- | ------- | -------- |
| `TicketEvent` | Product timeline (status, assign, priority, reopen) | Operator detail UI, optional member-visible subset |
| `AuditEvent` | Compliance / security (`entityType: Ticket`, `action: ticket.*`) | Existing audit trail — `schema.prisma:208-221` |

**INFERENCE:** `TicketEvent` rows are tenant-scoped and ticket-scoped; cheaper to query for UI than filtering global `AuditEvent`. `AuditEvent` remains the cross-entity compliance log.

**TicketEvent fields:**

| Field | Type | Notes |
| ----- | ---- | ----- |
| `id` | UUID | |
| `tenantId` | UUID | RLS |
| `ticketId` | UUID | |
| `actorUserId` | UUID | null for system |
| `eventType` | string | `status_changed`, `assigned`, `priority_changed`, `reopened` |
| `payload` | JSON | `{ from, to, ... }` |
| `createdAt` | timestamptz | |

**Member visibility:** Only `eventType` in allowlist (`status_changed`, `reopened`) with sanitized payload — no internal assignee notes in member view.

### 7.4 Future: TicketAttachment (Phase 7 — contract only)

**OUT OF SCOPE** implementation. Reserved design:

| Field | Notes |
| ----- | ----- |
| `storageKey` | `tickets/{tenantId}/{ticketId}/{uuid}/{safeFileName}` — pattern from `receipt-proof-storage.ts:30-36` |
| `contentType` | allowlist: jpeg, png, webp, pdf |
| `sizeBytes` | max 8 MiB (align receipt proof) |
| `uploadedByUserId` | |

---

## 8. Status lifecycle

### 8.1 Status enum (MVP)

| Status | Meaning | Member-visible label (fa) |
| ------ | ------- | --------------------------- |
| `open` | Active; team or member action needed | «باز» |
| `pending_member` | Waiting for member reply (Zendesk Pending) | «در انتظار پاسخ شما» |
| `resolved` | Operator sent resolution; member may reopen | «حل‌شده» |
| `closed` | Terminal for member; operator may reopen | «بسته» |

**DECISION:** No separate `awaiting_operator`. When member replies or creates ticket, status is `open`. Operator sets `pending_member` when waiting on member.

**DECISION:** No `new` or `on_hold`.

### 8.2 Creation and reply rules

| Event | New status | Actor |
| ----- | ---------- | ----- |
| Member creates ticket | `open` | system |
| Member posts public message (from `open`) | `open` | system |
| Member posts public message (from `pending_member`) | `open` | system |
| Member posts public message (from `resolved`) | `open` (+ reopen event) | system |
| Member posts public message (from `closed`) | **409** | — |
| Operator public reply (from `open`) | `open` (or `pending_member` if operator chooses) | operator |
| Operator sets awaiting member | `pending_member` | admin/owner |
| Operator sends resolution | `resolved` | admin/owner |
| Operator closes | `closed` | admin/owner |
| Member reopen (from `resolved`) | `open` | member |
| Operator/owner reopen (from `closed`) | `open` | admin/owner |

### 8.3 Transition matrix

Rows = **from**, columns = **to**. Cell = allowed actors.

| From \ To | open | pending_member | resolved | closed |
| --------- | ---- | -------------- | -------- | ------ |
| **open** | — | operator | operator | operator |
| **pending_member** | member, operator | — | operator | operator |
| **resolved** | member, operator | operator | — | operator |
| **closed** | operator, owner | — | — | — |

**Implicit transitions (not in PATCH body):**

- Member message from `resolved` → `open` (reopen)
- Member message from `pending_member` → `open`
- Operator public reply does not auto-change status unless PATCH accompanies

### 8.4 Resolved vs closed

**DECISION (Zendesk-aligned):**

- `resolved` = soft close; member can reply to reopen → `open`.
- `closed` = terminal for member; only operator/owner can reopen.
- No auto-close timer in MVP (Zendesk auto-close after 4 days — **OUT OF SCOPE** Phase 7).

### 8.5 Concurrency

| Scenario | Handling |
| -------- | -------- |
| Duplicate submit (create/message) | `Idempotency-Key` header → `HttpIdempotencyRecord` pattern |
| Concurrent status PATCH | `rowVersion` optimistic lock → **409** `TICKET_VERSION_CONFLICT` |
| Concurrent operator assign | Last-write-wins + `TicketEvent` |
| Message ordering | `createdAt` ASC; tie-break `id` |

---

## 9. Permission matrix

**DECISION:** All permissions enforced in `ticketing-core` + API routes. UI hiding is not sufficient.

Legend: ✅ allowed · ❌ denied · 🔒 own only · 👁 read-only

| Operation | member | viewer | admin | owner | platform admin |
| --------- | ------ | ------ | ----- | ----- | -------------- |
| Create ticket | ✅ | ❌ | ✅ | ✅ | ❌ |
| List own tickets | ✅ 🔒 | ✅ 🔒 | — | — | ❌ |
| List tenant tickets | ❌ | ❌ | ✅ | ✅ | ❌ |
| Read ticket | ✅ 🔒 | 👁 🔒 | ✅ | ✅ | ❌ |
| Public reply | ✅ 🔒 | ❌ | ✅ | ✅ | ❌ |
| Internal note | ❌ | ❌ | ✅ | ✅ | ❌ |
| Change status | ❌ | ❌ | ✅ | ✅ | ❌ |
| Change priority | ❌ | ❌ | ✅ | ✅ | ❌ |
| Assign | ❌ | ❌ | ✅ | ✅ | ❌ |
| Reopen from `resolved` | ✅ 🔒 | ❌ | ✅ | ✅ | ❌ |
| Reopen from `closed` | ❌ | ❌ | ✅ | ✅ | ❌ |
| Close | ❌ | ❌ | ✅ | ✅ | ❌ |
| Archive/delete | ❌ | ❌ | ❌ | ✅ | ❌ |
| Attachment access | ❌ MVP | ❌ | ❌ | ❌ | ❌ |

**CASL mapping:**

- Member routes: JWT with `role` in `member` | `viewer`; `viewer` is read-only subset.
- Operator routes: `requireOperatorSession` + `canPerformOperatorSurface('operator.tickets.*')`.
- `viewer` on Portal: same session as member but mutation endpoints return **403** `TICKET_VIEWER_READ_ONLY`.

**Priority change:** admin, owner only (not member).

---

## 10. API contract

### 10.1 Conventions

**FACT:** Project uses plain Node HTTP dispatch — `apps/api/src/app.ts`. Member upstream paths use `/member/*` (e.g. `/member/notifications` line 491). Wallet member paths use `/wallet/me/*` upstream — `apps/portal/app/api/me/wallet/route.ts:48`.

**DECISION:** Ticketing member upstream base: `/member/tickets` (consistent with `/member/notifications`). Operator: `/tickets` (consistent with `/bookings`).

**DECISION:** Portal BFF mirrors wallet: `/api/me/tickets/*` → upstream `/member/tickets/*` with `buildMemberApiHeaders` + tenant host binding — `apps/portal/app/api/me/wallet/route.ts:31-38`.

### 10.2 Member API (upstream)

Auth: JWT Bearer (`resolveTenantContextFromRequest`). Role: `member` or `viewer` (viewer = read-only).

#### `GET /member/tickets`

| Aspect | Detail |
| ------ | ------ |
| Auth | JWT; `member` or `viewer` |
| Query | `status?`, `cursor?`, `limit?` (default 20, max 50) |
| Output | `{ items: TicketSummary[], nextCursor?: string }` |
| Filter | `requesterUserId = auth.userId` always |
| Isolation | `tenantId` from JWT |
| Errors | 401 unauthorized |

#### `POST /member/tickets`

| Aspect | Detail |
| ------ | ------ |
| Auth | JWT; `member` only (viewer → 403) |
| Body | `{ categoryCode, subject, body, relatedTourId?, relatedRegistrationId? }` |
| Validation | Zod; subject 3-200; body 1-10000; categoryCode in manifest allowlist |
| Output | `{ ticket: TicketDetail }` (includes first message) |
| Idempotency | **Required** `Idempotency-Key` header |
| Side effect | Creates ticket `open` + first `TicketMessage` + `TicketEvent` |
| Errors | 400 validation, 403 viewer, 409 duplicate idempotency replay |

#### `GET /member/tickets/:ticketId`

| Aspect | Detail |
| ------ | ------ |
| Auth | JWT; member/viewer |
| Output | `TicketDetail` + `messages[]` (public only) + `events[]` (allowlist) |
| Isolation | `tenantId` + `requesterUserId` |
| Errors | 404 not found (no leak) |

#### `POST /member/tickets/:ticketId/messages`

| Aspect | Detail |
| ------ | ------ |
| Auth | JWT; `member` only |
| Body | `{ body }` |
| Idempotency | **Required** `Idempotency-Key` |
| Output | `{ message: TicketMessage }` |
| Errors | 409 `TICKET_CLOSED`, 403 viewer |

#### `POST /member/tickets/:ticketId/reopen`

| Aspect | Detail |
| ------ | ------ |
| Auth | JWT; `member` only |
| Precondition | `status = resolved` only |
| Body | optional `{ body }` — if present, creates message + reopen |
| Output | `{ ticket: TicketDetail }` |
| Errors | 409 if `closed` or `open` |

### 10.3 Operator API

Auth: `requireOperatorSession` + `operator.tickets.read` / `operator.tickets.mutate`.

#### `GET /tickets`

| Aspect | Detail |
| ------ | ------ |
| Query | `status?`, `priority?`, `categoryCode?`, `assigneeUserId?`, `unassigned?`, `q?`, `cursor?`, `limit?` |
| Output | `{ items: TicketSummary[], nextCursor? }` |
| Sort | `lastActivityAt` desc |
| Isolation | `tenantId` from JWT |

#### `GET /tickets/:ticketId`

| Aspect | Detail |
| ------ | ------ |
| Output | Full detail + all messages + events + requester summary |

#### `POST /tickets/:ticketId/replies`

| Aspect | Detail |
| ------ | ------ |
| Body | `{ body }` |
| Creates | `TicketMessage` visibility `public` |
| Errors | 409 `TICKET_CLOSED` |

#### `POST /tickets/:ticketId/internal-notes`

| Aspect | Detail |
| ------ | ------ |
| Body | `{ body }` |
| Creates | `TicketMessage` visibility `internal` |
| Auth | `operator.tickets.mutate` |

#### `PATCH /tickets/:ticketId`

| Aspect | Detail |
| ------ | ------ |
| Body | `{ status?, priority?, assigneeUserId?, rowVersion }` |
| Concurrency | `rowVersion` required → 409 on mismatch |
| Validation | Transition matrix §8.3; assignee membership |
| Output | `{ ticket: TicketDetail }` |

#### `POST /tickets/:ticketId/reopen`

| Aspect | Detail |
| ------ | ------ |
| Precondition | `status = closed` |
| Auth | admin/owner |
| Output | `{ ticket: TicketDetail }` status `open` |

### 10.4 Error codes

| Code | HTTP | When |
| ---- | ---- | ---- |
| `TICKET_NOT_FOUND` | 404 | No row or wrong tenant/owner |
| `TICKET_CLOSED` | 409 | Message on closed |
| `TICKET_VIEWER_READ_ONLY` | 403 | Viewer mutation |
| `TICKET_VERSION_CONFLICT` | 409 | rowVersion mismatch |
| `TICKET_INVALID_TRANSITION` | 409 | Status matrix violation |
| `TICKET_ASSIGNEE_INVALID` | 400 | Assignee not in tenant |
| `TICKET_CATEGORY_INVALID` | 400 | Unknown/disabled categoryCode |
| `TICKET_STORAGE_UNAVAILABLE` | 503 | Memory driver / no DATABASE_URL |

### 10.5 Portal BFF routes

| BFF | Upstream | Pattern source |
| --- | -------- | ---------------- |
| `GET /api/me/tickets` | `GET /member/tickets` | wallet BFF |
| `POST /api/me/tickets` | `POST /member/tickets` | |
| `GET /api/me/tickets/[ticketId]` | `GET /member/tickets/:id` | |
| `POST /api/me/tickets/[ticketId]/messages` | `POST /member/tickets/:id/messages` | |
| `POST /api/me/tickets/[ticketId]/reopen` | `POST /member/tickets/:id/reopen` | |

**FACT:** BFF validates `x-tenant-id` vs bootstrap tenant — `apps/portal/app/api/me/wallet/route.ts:37-38`.

